            <label lang="en">CH2_Ref</label>
            <description lang="en" />
            <denotation>
              <label lang="en" />
            </denotation>
            <defaultValue value="0" />
          </parameter>
          <parameter uniqueID="UID_PARAM_6421" access="read">
            <label lang="en">ErrorOutput</label>
            <description lang="en">Documentation for Error Messages

Error Messages are sent through TXPDO (TPDO[1]) every 100 ms. TXPDO[1] use 3 bytes to send three types of error: Errors on EV1, EV2 and errors on DIGITAL Output.
Each variable is a UINT8. ErrorOutput is a RAM only variables array with read-only capability.


See each variable description for more details.</description>
            <denotation>
              <label lang="en" />
            </denotation>
            <defaultValue value="" />
          </parameter>
          <parameter uniqueID="UID_PARAM_642100" access="read">
            <label lang="en">max sub-index</label>
            <description lang="en" />
            <denotation>
              <label lang="en" />
            </denotation>
            <defaultValue value="3" />
          </parameter>
          <parameter uniqueID="UID_PARAM_642101" access="read">
            <label lang="en">ErrorEV1</label>
            <description lang="en">TXPDO Mapping on Slot 0x1801 SubID 0.
Bit Position: Error Type

4: VSUPPLY_ERR
3: CAN_BUS_ERR
2: CC_ERR
1: OC_ERR
0: I_MAX_ERR

The error message is constructed by evaluating the corresponding bit positions in the error variables and assigning the appropriate values to each bit. By checking the state of these bits, you can determine which specific errors are present in the system.

VSUPPLY_ERR: Supply Voltage Error

Bit position: 4
Description: Represents an error related to the supply voltage. It indicates that there is an issue with the power supply voltage for the valve.
CAN_BUS_ERR: CAN Bus Connection Error

Bit position: 3
Description: Represents an error related to the CAN bus connection. It indicates that there is a problem with the communication on the CAN bus, which is used for data exchange between devices.
CC_ERR: Short Circuit Error

Bit position: 2
Description: Represents an error related to a short circuit. It indicates that a short circuit has been detected in the valve circuitry or wiring.
OC_ERR: Open Circuit Error

Bit position: 1
Description: Represents an error related to an open circuit. It indicates that an open circuit has been detected in the valve circuitry or wiring, causing a loss of continuity.
I_MAX_ERR: Maximum Current Reached Error

Bit position: 0
Description: Represents an error related to the maximum current threshold being reached. It indicates that the current flowing through the valve has exceeded the specified maximum limit.


</description>
            <denotation>
              <label lang="en" />
            </denotation>
            <defaultValue value="0" />
          </parameter>
          <parameter uniqueID="UID_PARAM_642102" access="read">
            <label lang="en">ErrorEV2</label>
            <description lang="en">TXPDO Mapping on Slot 0x1801 SubID 1.
Bit Position: Error Type

4: VSUPPLY_ERR
3: CAN_BUS_ERR
2: CC_ERR
1: OC_ERR
0: I_MAX_ERR

The error message is constructed by evaluating the corresponding bit positions in the error variables and assigning the appropriate values to each bit. By checking the state of these bits, you can determine which specific errors are present in the system.

VSUPPLY_ERR: Supply Voltage Error

Bit position: 4
Description: Represents an error related to the supply voltage. It indicates that there is an issue with the power supply voltage for the valve.
CAN_BUS_ERR: CAN Bus Connection Error

Bit position: 3
Description: Represents an error related to the CAN bus connection. It indicates that there is a problem with the communication on the CAN bus, which is used for data exchange between devices.
CC_ERR: Short Circuit Error

Bit position: 2
Description: Represents an error related to a short circuit. It indicates that a short circuit has been detected in the valve circuitry or wiring.
OC_ERR: Open Circuit Error

Bit position: 1
Description: Represents an error related to an open circuit. It indicates that an open circuit has been detected in the valve circuitry or wiring, causing a loss of continuity.
I_MAX_ERR: Maximum Current Reached Error

Bit position: 0
Description: Represents an error related to the maximum current threshold being reached. It indicates that the current flowing through the valve has exceeded the specified maximum limit.


</description>
            <denotation>
              <label lang="en" />
            </denotation>
            <defaultValue value="0" />
          </parameter>
          <parameter uniqueID="UID_PARAM_642103" access="read">
            <label lang="en">ErrorDigital</label>
            <description lang="en">TXPDO Mapping on Slot 0x1801 SubID 2.
Object for digital Output Error Signaling. Used only if Number of digital output available is &gt; 0.
Each bits indicates if a specific digital output detects Short Circuit or not.

0b01 - Short Circuit detected.
0b00 - No short circuit detected.

E.g.

ErrorDigital= 0b00100100   
Short circuit detected on digital output [3] and [6].</description>
            <denotation>
              <label lang="en" />
            </denotation>
            <defaultValue value="0" />
          </parameter>
          <parameter uniqueID="UID_PARAM_6431" access="readWrite">
            <label lang="en">DigitalOutput</label>
            <description lang="en">Object for digital Output Values Feedback. Used only if Number of digital output available is &gt; 0.
Each bits indicates if a specific digital output is active or not.

TXPDO Mapping over Slot 0x1802 - SubID 0.

0b01 - Digital Output Active
0b00 - Digital Output Not Active

E.g.

DigitalOutput = 0b00100100   
Digital output [3] and [6] are active.</description>
            <denotation>
              <label lang="en" />
            </denotation>
            <defaultValue value="0" />
          </parameter>
          <parameter uniqueID="UID_PARAM_6441" access="readWrite">
            <label lang="en">DigitalInput</label>
            <description lang="en">Object for digital Output Values Control. Used only if Number of digital output available is &gt; 0.
Each bits operates on a specific digital output to activate or deactivate it.
RXPDO Mapping over Slot 0x1402 subID 1.

0b01 - Activate Digital Output
0b00 - Deactivate Digital Output

E.g.

DigitalOutput = 0b00100100   
Digital output [3] and [6] are active.</description>
            <denotation>
              <label lang="en" />
            </denotation>
            <defaultValue value="0" />
          </parameter>
        </parameterList>
      </ApplicationProcess>
    </ProfileBody>
